  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FTF Bangladesh Inclusive Access to Finance Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  The FTF Bangladesh Inclusive Access to Finance activity will facilitate increased access to finance for agricultural micro, small, and medium enterprises (MSMEs) and smallholder farmers. With FY 2024 funds, the activity will work on the supply and demand sides of the market for financing. On the supply side, the activity will partner with banks, microfinance institutions, non-bank financial institutions, and village savings and loan associations to create new blended finance products for target populations and sectors. The activity will also work with financial institutions to develop new loan products tailored to the needs of USAID&apos;s target populations, and to strengthen their knowledge of USAID&apos;s priority sectors. On the demand side of the market, USAID will help prospective borrowers become more creditworthy through targeted training and assistance. The activity will make special efforts to increase lending to priority populations and sectors, including women and youth, first-time borrowers, and farmers and businesses investing in climate-smart agricultural techniques. As a result of the investments facilitated by the activity, MSMEs and farmers will increase their productivity, invest in climate-smart agricultural techniques, and become more incorporated into the formal financial system. The activity supports the Global Food Security Strategy. Funding for the activity contributes to the  Global Food Security ($3.7m), Gender Equality and Women Empowerment Secondary ($700k), Private Sector Engagement ($1m), MSME (300k) directives and key issues.</narrative>
  </description>
